hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16","The respected wife of Uthman bin Maz'oon, Sayyida Khawla bint Hakim (may Allah be pleased with her), narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out along with Hasan and Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he said: “(Children) become a cause of miserliness and cowardice for a person.” And on another occasion, when she narrated, she said: I saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: “And you people act with miserliness.”"
"17","Sayyida Khawla (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The last trampling which your Lord decreed took place in Waj (the valley of Ta’if)."""
